# Deny-by-default: everything at the repository root is ignored, then the
# directories and files Tutre actually tracks are re-allowed below.
# Adding a new top-level file? Add a matching `!` line or git will not see it.
# Check with: git check-ignore -v <path>
/*

# Applications
!/admin-panel/
!/student-panel/

# Backend: Supabase CLI config, migrations, Edge Functions
!/supabase/

# Project documentation and agent configuration
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.gitignore
!/.claude/

# Generated code-graph analysis output (tracked deliberately)
!/graphify-out/

# Never track secrets, anywhere, at any depth
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
